            <div xml:id="d367-a2">

                <pb facs="0490" n="410" xml:id="pg410"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. de Lafayette, and, with appropriate
                        changes, to Count de Rochambeau</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-03-27"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Animated by a sense of profound gratitude
                    for the inestimable services rendered to the United States during their war of
                    revolution by your renowned ancestor, the Congress of the United States, by a
                    joint resolutiou of March 21, 1902, authorized and requested the President to
                    extend to the family of the Marquis de Lafayette a cordial invitation to unite
                    with the Government and people of the United States in a fit and appropriate
                    dedication of the monument of Marshal de Rochambeau to be unveiled in the city
                    of Washington on May 24, 1902.</p>
                <p>It is with more than ordinary pleasure that I fulfill the duty of transmitting
                    this invitation to you and through you to the family of the Marquis de
                    Lafayette.</p>
                <p>I have instructed the ambassador of the United States at Paris to convey this to
                    you in a fitting manner, and to say that the members of this illustrious family
                    who may do us the honor to visit the United States upon this occasion will be
                    welcomed as guests of the nation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
